.th CPIO V 5/31/77
.sh NAME
cpio \*- format of cpio archive
.sh SYNOPSIS
.tr _\(ul
.nf
.ft B
struct {
	int	h_magic,
		h_dev,
		h_ino,
		h_mode,
		h_uid,
		h_gid,
		h_nlink,
		h_majmin;
	long	h_mtime;
	int	h_namesize;
	long	h_filesize;
	char	h_name[h_namesize rounded to word];
	char	data[h_filesize rounded to word];
} archive;
.ft R
.fi
.sh DESCRIPTION
The
.it contents
of each file is recorded in an element
of the array of varying length structures,
.it archive,
together with other items describing the file.
Every instance of 
.it h_magic
contains the constant 070707.
The items
.it h_dev
through 
.it h_mtime
have meanings explained in
.it stat\^\c
(II).
The length of the null-terminated pathname
.it h_name,
including the null byte,
is given by
.it h_namesize.
.s3
The last record
of the
.it archive
always contains the name `TRAILER!!!'.
Special files, directories, and the trailer are recorded
with 
.it
h_filesize
= 0.
.sh "SEE ALSO"
cpio(I), stat(II)
.sh BUGS
This format should be reconciled with
.it archive\^\c
(V).
.tr __
